  "ref": "JOB.2.3",
  "review_notes": [
    "שַׂמְתָּ לִבְּךָ is fused as one two-morpheme unit rendered *considered* (rule 30), with the suffix on לֵב unrepresented; the alternative would strand the verb or the noun with no rendering.",
    "Both indefinite articles of *a perfect and an upright man* are given to אִישׁ under rule 15; the note on that unit records the distributive alternative.",
    "The concessive *although* is placed on the waw of וַתְּסִיתֵנִי, matching the ASV margin's *Or, that*, which is a competing connective for the same morpheme."
  ]
